'' docs/tiko-properties R8 ACROSS A MODULE INTERFACE. The interface carries each TYPE verbatim, its
'' accessor clauses with it, and leaves the synthesised bodies out (TF_AUTOPROP, tkiemit.tiko): the
'' importer writes its own and the weak copies fold -- a generic type's included, whose members are
'' otherwise written whole. A private setter stays private to the module's own methods; a static one's
'' storage folds too (R11).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -i tests/modules/src/autoprop/libs tests/modules/src/autoprop/app/main.tiko -o tests/modules/autoprop.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: duplicate symbol
'' RUN: tests/modules/autoprop.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: pt 42
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: q 42
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  7 vw 6
